From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:38:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: unregister leftover vblank callbacks at unload

nv_drm_crtc_destroy() frees the CRTC without unregistering its NVKMS vblank
interrupt callback; only the disable_vblank work does that. Before unload
the callback is normally gone because the fbdev shutdown commit
(drm_atomic_helper_shutdown) calls drm_crtc_vblank_off() for every active
CRTC, which queues that work while the vblank worker still runs.

Without fbdev (nvidia-drm.fbdev=0) there is no such commit: the CRTCs stay
active with vblank enabled, the DRM vblank disable timer can no longer queue
the work once nv_drm_workthread_shutdown() has run, and drm_mode_config_cleanup()
frees the CRTCs while NVKMS still holds callbacks pointing at them. A vblank
before nvKms->freeDevice() then runs nv_drm_crtc_vblank_callback() on freed
memory.

After stopping the vblank worker, run the disable work directly for every
CRTC: it unregisters a callback that is still registered and completes any
flip events waiting for a vblank. Stopping the worker first ensures no queued
enable registers the callback again afterwards. The unregister ioctl takes
nvkms_lock under nv_dev->lock, as declareEventInterest() already does here;
NVKMS delivers events and vblank callbacks without taking nv_dev->lock.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h |  2 ++
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c  |  6 ++++++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 69e37fb8..70331cc6 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -3724,6 +3724,19 @@ static void nv_drm_vblank_disable_fn(void *t)
     mutex_unlock(&nv_crtc->vblank_q_lock);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Unregister the NVKMS vblank callback if it is still registered at device
+ * teardown. Only the fbdev shutdown commit turns vblank off before unload,
+ * and once the vblank worker is stopped the disable work can't be queued
+ * anymore, so without this the callback would outlive the CRTC it points
+ * to. Call after the vblank worker is stopped and before the CRTCs are
+ * destroyed.
+ */
+void nv_drm_crtc_vblank_teardown(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc)
+{
+    nv_drm_vblank_disable_fn(nv_crtc);
+}
+
 /*
  * Add drm crtc for given head and supported enum NvKmsSurfaceMemoryFormats.
  */
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
index 2d34b9c9..8ee71975 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.h
@@ -373,6 +373,8 @@ bool nv_drm_crtc_defer_flip_to_pending(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
 void nv_drm_crtc_set_vblank_duration(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc,
                                      const struct drm_crtc_state *crtc_state);
 
+void nv_drm_crtc_vblank_teardown(struct nv_drm_crtc *nv_crtc);
+
 /*
  * CRTCs are static objects, list does not change once after initialization and
  * before teardown of device. Initialization/teardown paths are single
diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
index ff99ada9..7b979153 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-drv.c
@@ -983,7 +983,13 @@ static void nv_drm_dev_unload(struct drm_device *dev)
     drm_kms_helper_poll_fini(dev);
 
     if (nv_drm_vblank_module_param) {
+        struct drm_crtc *crtc;
+
         nv_drm_workthread_shutdown(&nv_dev->vblank_worker);
+
+        nv_drm_for_each_crtc(crtc, dev) {
+            nv_drm_crtc_vblank_teardown(to_nv_crtc(crtc));
+        }
     }
 
     nv_drm_held_fbs_fini(nv_dev);
